One events resource object: a standard whose number was changed.

Verbatim from a live sample, gate G-4 result in 01-sdk-v3.md section 12, run 2026-08-02 against devel
partner sws:

  {"name":"number.raw","previous_value":"a.","new_value":"MU:CT.HSAdv.Pr4.a"} on an
  "updated numbering"/standard event

The affected_properties element is that capture, unchanged, and so are the change_type and target. It
is the second of the two G-4 affected_properties samples, kept separate from the first because here
previous_value and new_value are JSON strings rather than JSON numbers: one fixture proves
AffectedProperty.NewValue survives as a number, the other proves it survives as a string, and together
they justify JsonElement over any concrete type.

Verbatim: the "standard" relationship id 26998816-1a35-11eb-bb5b-0e20088bb29a is the id G-4 captured
on a live event, in the lower case AB Connect returned it in. Note that the attributes.guid in this
fixture is the same GUID in upper case, which is how AB Connect spells standard GUIDs elsewhere. The
case difference is real and is documented on ABEvent.Id: never compare the two forms without
normalizing case.

Assembled for this fixture, not observed live: the event id, seq, date_utc, document_guid, and
section_guid.
